  "notes": [
    "48 skills, each with the 1–2 weighted stats the Skills tab gives it. Single-stat skills weigh 0.2 or 0.3; two-stat skills split 0.2 + 0.1.",
    "Since TICKET-SKL-02 the weights are the stored shape: `statWeights: [{ statId, weight }]`, keyed by stat id. The numbers are unchanged — they were already the sheet's, encoded as a `bonusFormula` string — but the app now holds them as data rather than as an opaque expression, which is Concept 02's whole argument. The level is Σ(weight × stat) + invested and the bonus is round(level / const.bonus_divider); neither is per-skill any more, so this fragment needs stats.json and constants.json loaded alongside it.",
    "`maxBaseLevel` and the 3-letter `code` are **gone**. The sheet has no level cap, and the code only ever existed so a formula could name a skill in the flat variable space — a formula reaches one as `skills.<name-slug>` now, so there is nothing left for a code to do.",
    "Duplicate name kept deliberately (Concept 02 import note): Skinning appears twice in the sheet with different levels, so they are two records until the User merges them. They slug the same way, so the first one wins any `skills.skinning` reference — which is exactly the ambiguity the merge is there to settle.",
    "Verified against Concept 02: Charm = CHA × 0.3 (11.7 at Char 39), Brewing = WIS × 0.3, Black smithing = STR × 0.2, alchemy = INT × 0.2, Trading = CHA × 0.3.",
    "One divergence from Concept 02, and the sheet wins: the page has Persuasion at Char × 0.3, the live Skills tab has Char × 0.2 + Strenght × 0.1 (Skills!D31:G31). The page's 11.7 for Persuasion is Charm's number. SETTLED by TICKET-DX-04: the golden suite pins Persuasion at 8.8 (the live weights, range cited) and pins the page's 13.2 -> bonus 3 on Charm, where the weights that produce it live, with the inferred +1.5 tagged as inferred."
  ],
